  "_doc": "The player model AND its hit geometry: the client draws every part (web/assets/models/player.js) and the server ray-traces every part with hit != false (internal/game/hitbox.go), both posed by the same function of the replicated state (pos, yaw, pitch, crouch). Boxes: c = centre, s = full size (metres), in the player's frame (feet at the origin, -Z forward); 'crouch' overrides c/s when crouched. Parts with 'pivot' are rotated by the view pitch about that point (c is then relative to the pivot). region picks the damage multiplier; team limits a part to one team's outfit. color: a palette name, 'team', or 'team*k' for a shade. Per-player variation is seeded by player id (web/gen/boxmodel.js): 'vars' are drawn in order from rng(seed + id), then each 'jitter' part's offsets in part order; 'when' {var: min} shows a part only if that var is at least min; 'vary' {var: {c, s}} adds var x vector to the centre and size; 'jitter' adds \u00b1that to the centre. team may also be a list ('' = teamless). color may be a {team: spec, '*': spec} map; a spec is a palette name, 'team'/'player' (personal colour) or 'rgb' (cycling), times factors that are numbers or var names ('artisanWool*wool*0.85').",
